::Full Stack Developer Definition::
A full stack developer is someone who:
{
~ Specializes only in front-end development
~ Specializes only in back-end development
= Is knowledgeable in both front-end and back-end development
~ Works only with databases and servers
}

::Front End vs Back End (T/F)::
The front end of an application refers to everything that the user can see and interact with. 
{
T
}

::Real World Analogy::
In the restaurant analogy used to describe full stack development, the kitchen and pantry represent which part of the system?
{
~ Front end
= Back end
~ User interface
~ Decor and seating areas
}
